---
// desire-not-plumbing — the one idea that makes melanocortin sexual pharmacology
// make sense. Two drugs act on two different points of the same act. A
// melanocortin agonist (bremelanotide) works in the BRAIN, on MC4R circuits
// that generate desire and arousal — upstream, the "wanting". A PDE5 inhibitor
// (sildenafil) works in the PERIPHERY, on blood flow in the genitals —
// downstream, the "plumbing", and only once arousal is already present. One
// starts the signal; the other carries out an order it did not give.
// Schematic; SVG-only, wrap in <Figure>.
---

<svg
  class="dnp-fig"
  viewBox="0 0 640 316"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="dnp-t dnp-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="dnp-t">Two drugs, two points in the same act: desire versus plumbing</title>
  <desc id="dnp-d"
    >Melanocortin agonists such as bremelanotide act centrally, in the brain, on
    MC4R circuits that generate sexual desire and arousal — the upstream signal,
    the wanting. PDE5 inhibitors such as sildenafil act peripherally, on blood
    flow in the genitals — the downstream mechanics, and only once arousal is
    already present. One starts the signal; the other carries out the order.</desc
  >

  <!-- brain / central column -->
  <rect class="col accent" x="20" y="44" width="286" height="236" rx="14" />
  <text x="40" y="76" class="col-h accent-t">In the brain — the signal</text>
  <text x="40" y="96" class="col-sub">central · MC4R</text>

  <rect class="node accent" x="40" y="116" width="246" height="56" rx="10" />
  <text x="56" y="140" class="node-t accent-t">MC4R circuits fire</text>
  <text x="56" y="158" class="node-s">desire &amp; arousal are generated</text>

  <path class="flow accent-flow" d="M163 172 V200" marker-end="url(#dnp-arr-a)" />

  <rect class="node" x="40" y="202" width="246" height="56" rx="10" />
  <text x="56" y="226" class="node-t">the “wanting” begins</text>
  <text x="56" y="244" class="node-s">bremelanotide · melanotan act here</text>

  <!-- divider arrow: desire leads to arousal leads to response -->
  <path class="bridge" d="M306 160 H334" marker-end="url(#dnp-arr)" />
  <text x="320" y="150" text-anchor="middle" class="bridge-t">then</text>

  <!-- body / peripheral column -->
  <rect class="col" x="334" y="44" width="286" height="236" rx="14" />
  <text x="354" y="76" class="col-h">In the bloodstream — the plumbing</text>
  <text x="354" y="96" class="col-sub">peripheral · PDE5</text>

  <rect class="node" x="354" y="116" width="246" height="56" rx="10" />
  <text x="370" y="140" class="node-t">blood flow responds</text>
  <text x="370" y="158" class="node-s">only if arousal is already present</text>

  <path class="flow" d="M477 172 V200" marker-end="url(#dnp-arr)" />

  <rect class="node" x="354" y="202" width="246" height="56" rx="10" />
  <text x="370" y="226" class="node-t">the mechanics follow</text>
  <text x="370" y="244" class="node-s">sildenafil (Viagra) acts here</text>

  <defs>
    <marker id="dnp-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--text-muted)" />
    </marker>
    <marker id="dnp-arr-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--accent)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>
</svg>

<style>
